Token-like literals observed are synthetic fixture values old-access/old-refresh/access/the-refresh-token, never provider credentials.
Source inspection: tokens read independently through AuthLocalDataSource (ITokenStore boundary); no new disk persistence; local clear and HTTP cache clear precede remote await; local error wins.
Remote access snapshot appears only in Authorization header; refresh snapshot only in refresh_token body. Existing ApiLoggingInterceptor redacts Authorization case-insensitively and refresh-token keys.
AuthInterceptor stamps request generation; rejects stale first send after async store read and stale retry before auth; logout excluded from refresh recursion.
Sign-in waits on tracked logout future, so a new session cannot land during old revocation; snapshot cannot switch identity mid-request.
Only production changes are auth repository, auth remote datasource signature/header, and demo signature; no dependencies, transport platforms or RASP behavior changed.
Optional accessToken parameter requires custom datasource implementers to update their override; parent notified to include adopter migration note in Unreleased before closure.
